<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The intuition behind the bookkeeping strategy
can be understood through
the invariant condition
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> proved in <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Namely, one unit of bookkeeping mass is partitioned into a
shared portion of size <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, associated with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and, for each unresolved
round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, a reserved portion of size <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\tau,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\tau,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with the
historical weight vector <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\tau,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\tau,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is reduced to
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\tau,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\tau,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the difference
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\tau,t}=a_{\tau,t-1}-a_{\tau,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\tau,t}=a_{\tau,t-1}-a_{\tau,t}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes available for forming the
current weight vector <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the portion <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\tau,t}w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\tau,t}w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> remains
reserved for round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. The new round then reserves the portion
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,t}w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,t}w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for its own future feedback. Once the feedback from round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>
arrives, its reserved portion is updated using the corresponding historical
weight vector <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and returned to the shared component <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this way, the delayed feedback can be applied to the weight vector that generated
the corresponding prediction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our algorithm also progressively refines the set of meta-experts <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure that each <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> uses a meta-learning rate
satisfying <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}/a_{s,t}\geq-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}/a_{s,t}\geq-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on all rounds.
In particular, recall that a key technical step in the usual Prod analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gaillard and Stoltz, 2014</a>)</cite> is to apply the so-called Prod bound:
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In our context, we want to apply this bound
to <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(u_{s,t}^{h}/w_{s}^{h})=\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{s}^{h}/a_{s,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(u_{s,t}^{h}/w_{s}^{h})=\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{s}^{h}/a_{s,t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which requires that we set <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\leq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}=\min_{s,t}a_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\leq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}=\min_{s,t}a_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> in general.
Yet <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is
generally not known at the start of the game, so the condition may not be ensured when <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>
is constructed.
Instead, starting from an initial set of meta-learning rates,
at the start of each round we prune all <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> that would not satisfy <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>
on all prior rounds (<a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithms</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#algorithm1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#algorithm1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). Crucially, we show in <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> that this
still results in a well-defined algorithm, and by round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> all remaining <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>
have step-sizes satisfying <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> on all rounds, allowing us to
derive the following second-order guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every base expert <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and every prior
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\operatorname{int}\Delta(\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\operatorname{int}\Delta(\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> guarantees
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\frac{\log(1/\rho^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\frac{\log(1/\rho^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The complete proof is deferred to <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. We sketch it here by
adapting the two steps of the standard ML-Prod analysis: a per-round inequality
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a telescoping
argument showing that these logarithmic increments sum to at most
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\rho^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\rho^{h})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under delayed feedback, both steps must be modified since the feedback associated
with round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is not available until round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+d_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+d_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
(see <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E A Brief Review of ML-Prod ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>
for more details).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">First, when the feedback of round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is eventually revealed, only an
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,t+d_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,t+d_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of its historical weight remains active. The
corrected update therefore satisfies
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(u_{t+d_{t}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})=\log(1+(\eta_{h}/a_{t,t+d_{t}})r_{t}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(u_{t+d_{t}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})=\log(1+(\eta_{h}/a_{t,t+d_{t}})r_{t}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying the usual ML-Prod logarithmic inequality and using
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,t+d_{t}}=1/\chi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,t+d_{t}}=1/\chi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> produces the desired second-order penalty
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}^{2}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}^{2}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Second, the residual vector <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> allows the delayed updates from
different rounds to telescope within a single potential. Let
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\left\langle\mathbf{1},F_{t}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\left\langle\mathbf{1},F_{t}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and define
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}^{h}\coloneq S_{t}\log(F_{t}^{h}/S_{t})+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}\log w_{\tau}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}^{h}\coloneq S_{t}\log(F_{t}^{h}/S_{t})+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}\log w_{\tau}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The construction of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that the weighted
log-ratios corresponding to all feedback revealed at round <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are
controlled by the increment <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t+1}^{h}-\Phi_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t+1}^{h}-\Phi_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing over time, and using the initialization <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>
leads to</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}+\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\log\frac{1}{\rho^{h}}+\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}+\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\log\frac{1}{\rho^{h}}+\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">which yields <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> holds for a fixed <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> whose best
value depends on the unknown excess losses and delays. To adapt to it, we use a geometric grid of learning-rate copies for each base algorithm.
Proof of the following result can be found in <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite collection of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> base algorithms, let
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\coloneq\lceil\log_{2}T\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\coloneq\lceil\log_{2}T\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}\coloneq 2^{-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}\coloneq 2^{-j}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the set of meta-experts
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}\coloneq\left\{(A,j):A\in\mathfrak{A},\ j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\coloneq\left\{(A,j):A\in\mathfrak{A},\ j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(A,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(A,j)</annotation></semantics></math> follows the decisions of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and uses the meta-learning rate
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\operatorname{int}\Delta(\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\operatorname{int}\Delta(\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> be the uniform
prior, i.e., <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{h}=1/\left|\mathcal{H}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{h}=1/\left|\mathcal{H}\right|</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with prior <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees</span></p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq 3\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}+3\sqrt{H_{\rho}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq 3\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}+3\sqrt{H_{\rho}\sum\limits_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}\coloneq\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}\coloneq\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, up to the additive <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> term,
<a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> attains the desired
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\big(\sqrt{\sum_{t}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\big(\sqrt{\sum_{t}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> bound with
<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no prior knowledge</em> of the delays. Combined with <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
this single guarantee suffices for universal regret under time-varying delays:
the first bound in <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> yields the <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{T+d_{\mathrm{tot}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{T+d_{\mathrm{tot}}}</annotation></semantics></math> rate for
general convex losses, while the second yields the <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}\log T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}\log T</annotation></semantics></math>
rates for strongly convex and exp-concave losses.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish universal regret guarantees under delayed feedback. We first develop an improved <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent regret guarantee for exp-concave losses, which will serve as one of the base learners in our universal construction. We then combine this algorithm with delayed OGD and delayed FTRL through the delayed meta-algorithm (<a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) from <a href="#S3" title="3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to obtain a single learner that adapts to general convex, strongly convex, and exp-concave losses that requires no preliminary knowledge about the loss geometry or delays.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by developing an improved Delay-Accounting ONS algorithm for
exp-concave losses with a known curvature parameter. This new algorithm carefully extends the weighting principle of Delayed ML-Prod to ONS
for exp-concave losses, as detailed in <a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. While Delayed ML-Prod weights
historical expert-weight vectors <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> weights historical
quadratic objectives <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, keeping each delayed update
tied to the objective that generated its prediction. Otherwise, the coefficients
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\tau,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\tau,t}</annotation></semantics></math> account for outstanding observations in the same
way as in <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
We also adapt the delay-adaptive
learning-rate tuning of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al. (2025)</a></cite> to obtain
both the <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent
regret bounds, as established in the following theorem.</p>
</div>
