<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Bounded domain and gradients). ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds and that every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-exp-concave (<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (𝛼-exp-concavity). ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
Let
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\coloneq\frac{1}{2}\min\left\{\frac{1}{4GD},\alpha\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\coloneq\frac{1}{2}\min\left\{\frac{1}{4GD},\alpha\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math> Run <a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with any <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}=G/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}=G/D</annotation></semantics></math>, and, for every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}=\eta_{0}+\min\Bigl\{\frac{\sigma_{t}n}{2\beta D^{2}}\log\Bigl(1+t+\frac{\beta GDt}{n}\Bigr),\frac{G}{D}\sqrt{1+\sum_{s=1}^{t}|m_{s}|}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>G</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}=\eta_{0}+\min\Bigl\{\frac{\sigma_{t}n}{2\beta D^{2}}\log\Bigl(1+t+\frac{\beta GDt}{n}\Bigr),\frac{G}{D}\sqrt{1+\sum_{s=1}^{t}|m_{s}|}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Then, for every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> guarantees that
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)=\mathcal{O}(\tfrac{1}{\beta}[n\log T+\min\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\}])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)=\mathcal{O}(\tfrac{1}{\beta}[n\log T+\min\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\}]).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Compared with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> replaces
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> in the logarithmic bound by the potentially
smaller <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, while retaining the
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}</annotation></semantics></math> dependence.
The proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> is deferred to
<a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. There are two main ingredients.
First, we use a potential argument similar to that for Delayed
ML-Prod, replacing scalar log-weights by log-determinants of
Hessians. The weighting allows delayed updates from different rounds
to telescope. Together with
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,t+d_{t}}=1/\chi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,t+d_{t}}=1/\chi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{t}\leq 1+\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{t}\leq 1+\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, this yields the
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent logarithmic bound.
Second, we control the delay-dependent terms using the number of missing observations and the learning-rate sequence. This gives a decomposition into a prefix term depending on <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and a suffix term depending on <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=\tau+1}^{T}|m_{t}|/\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=\tau+1}^{T}|m_{t}|/\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing the learning-rate sequence adaptively and selecting the splitting point <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> then yields the minimum of the <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent bounds stated in the theorem.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Universal Regret Guarantee</h3>

<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Universal OCO with Delayed Feedback</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
