<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Omitted Details from <a href="#S3" title="3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we restate <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, which shows the main regret bound of <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and provide its proof.
See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows a similar structure as the standard ML-Prod analysis
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gaillard and Stoltz, 2014</a>, Theorem 1]</cite>, which itself builds upon the Prod analysis of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cesa-Bianchi et al. [2007, Lemma 2]</a></cite>.
Here, given the presence of arbitrary delays, we require a specific cumulative control of the log-weight ratios as provided by <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> in addition to the carefully designed update rule of <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any expert <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any such meta-expert survives all rounds
without being retired, so
by <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{u_{t,t+d_{t}}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}=\log\left(1+\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{u_{t,t+d_{t}}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}=\log\left(1+\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,t+d_{t}}=\min_{s\in I_{t}}1/(1+\left|m_{s}\right|)=1/\chi_{t}\geq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,t+d_{t}}=\min_{s\in I_{t}}1/(1+\left|m_{s}\right|)=1/\chi_{t}\geq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, so together with <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\leq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\leq 1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t}^{h}\geq-1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{h}\geq-1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\geq-\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\geq-\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\geq-1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq-1/2</annotation></semantics></math>
(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cesa-Bianchi and Lugosi, 2006</a>, Lemma 2.4</cite>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t,t+d_{t}}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t,t+d_{t}}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\left(1+\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\left(1+\frac{\eta_{h}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}r_{t}^{h}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\frac{\eta_{h}^{2}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\frac{\eta_{h}^{2}}{a_{t,t+d_{t}}}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality again uses <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Summing the previous inequality over all rounds <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math> and applying <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}\leq\log\frac{1}{\rho^{h}}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}a_{t,t+d_{t}}\log\frac{u_{t}^{h}}{w_{t}^{h}}\leq\log\frac{1}{\rho^{h}}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging and dividing by <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given a base algorithm <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose any <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that this is always possible since
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{J}=2^{-J}\leq 1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{J}=2^{-J}\leq 1/T</annotation></semantics></math>, while
<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\max_{t}\left|m_{t}\right|\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\max_{t}\left|m_{t}\right|\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that for a fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, any two meta-experts <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,i)\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,i)\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> differ only in their
associated meta-learning rate and produce the same decisions on each round, and
therefore produce the same excess-loss sequence;
denote it by <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{t})_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{t})_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since these copies are assigned
equal prior mass, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\rho^{h})=\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)\eqcolon H_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\rho^{h})=\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)\eqcolon H_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> is also the same for all of them.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now since any such expert satisfying <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> survives all rounds without being retired,
we have by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\frac{\log(1/\rho^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}=\frac{H_{\rho}}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}V_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}\leq\frac{\log(1/\rho^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}=\frac{H_{\rho}}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}V_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we have defined <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}\coloneq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}\coloneq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the ideal meta-learning rate</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{*}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}^{+}},\sqrt{\frac{H_{\rho}}{V_{T}}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{*}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}^{+}},\sqrt{\frac{H_{\rho}}{V_{T}}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we define <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}/V_{T}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}/V_{T}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Observe that by definition, <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}\leq\frac{1}{4}\sigma_{\max}^{+}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}\leq\frac{1}{4}\sigma_{\max}^{+}T</annotation></semantics></math>,
and moreover for <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)\geq\log(J+1)\geq 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}=\log\bigl(N(J+1)\bigr)\geq\log(J+1)\geq 1/4</annotation></semantics></math>,
so</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{H_{\rho}}{V_{T}}}\geq\frac{2\sqrt{H_{\rho}}}{\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}T}}\geq\frac{1}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\frac{H_{\rho}}{V_{T}}}\geq\frac{2\sqrt{H_{\rho}}}{\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}T}}\geq\frac{1}{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\max_{t}\left|m_{t}\right|\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\max_{t}\left|m_{t}\right|\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, since <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have overall that
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}\in[1/T,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}\in[1/T,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, suppose we choose
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=\lceil\log_{2}(1/\eta^{*})\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=\lceil\log_{2}(1/\eta^{*})\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq j\leq J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq j\leq J</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\eta^{*}}{2}\leq\eta_{j}\leq\eta^{*}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}^{+}}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\eta^{*}}{2}\leq\eta_{j}\leq\eta^{*}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}^{+}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">so this expert is never retired and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> applies.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq\frac{H_{\rho}}{\eta_{j}}+\eta_{j}V_{T}\leq\frac{2H_{\rho}}{\eta^{*}}+\eta^{*}V_{T}\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq\frac{H_{\rho}}{\eta_{j}}+\eta_{j}V_{T}\leq\frac{2H_{\rho}}{\eta^{*}}+\eta^{*}V_{T}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Now if <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}=\sqrt{H_{\rho}/V_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}=\sqrt{H_{\rho}/V_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq 3\sqrt{H_{\rho}V_{T}}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq 3\sqrt{H_{\rho}V_{T}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">while if <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}=1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}=1/\sigma_{\max}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, its definition
implies that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}\leq(\sigma_{\max}^{+})^{2}H_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}\leq(\sigma_{\max}^{+})^{2}H_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>
so</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq 2\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}+\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}}(\sigma_{\max}^{+})^{2}H_{\rho}=3H_{\rho}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}\leq 2\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}+\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}}(\sigma_{\max}^{+})^{2}H_{\rho}=3H_{\rho}\sigma_{\max}^{+}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two cases yields the stated bound.
∎</span></p>
