<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Auxiliary Results for Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section derives several auxiliary results for <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
The first lemma provides some basic bookkeeping about invariant
properties of the algorithm. This will be used to
show that the algorithm is well-defined in <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
and to prove a delayed variant of the usual ML-Prod telescoping
identity in <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The following hold on every round <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(i)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{t}\geq 0\text{~~and~~}S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,t-1}=1;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{t}\geq 0\text{~~and~~}S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,t-1}=1;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(ii)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{t}=1-\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,t}\geq a_{t,t}&gt;0;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{t}=1-\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,t}\geq a_{t,t}&gt;0;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(iii)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{\tau,t}=\frac{1}{1+\max_{\tau\leq s\leq t}|m_{s}|},\quad\forall\,\tau\leq t\leq\tau+d_{\tau};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{\tau,t}=\frac{1}{1+\max_{\tau\leq s\leq t}|m_{s}|},\quad\forall\,\tau\leq t\leq\tau+d_{\tau};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(iv)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{t,t+d_{t}}=\frac{1}{\chi_{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{t,t+d_{t}}=\frac{1}{\chi_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the first round we have <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,
so <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Lemma 2. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> trivially holds.
Now assuming that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}+\sum_{\tau\in m_{t}}a_{\tau,{t-1}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> holds on round <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have by definition of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the fact that
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=m_{{t+1}}\cup\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=m_{{t+1}}\cup\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmlemma13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ Appendix D Supporting Lemmas ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) that</span></p>
