<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With the book-keeping lemma in hand, the following lemma
shows that <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is well defined.
The proof also proves some important properties of
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\tau,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\tau,t}</annotation></semantics></math> generated during the
execution of the algorithm, which will be important for
<a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ A.3 Auxiliary Results for Algorithm ‣ Appendix A Omitted Details from ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#algorithm1" title="In Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{h}\leq 1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{h}\leq 1/T</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined.
At round <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-empty,
and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(w_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(w_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t}=\left(\frac{\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}}{\sum_{k\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{k}w_{t}^{k}}\right)_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t}=\left(\frac{\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}}{\sum_{k\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{k}w_{t}^{k}}\right)_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defines a valid probability distribution on <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, for all <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> it holds that <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(F_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(F_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
and for every <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\tau,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\tau,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(u_{\tau,t})=\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(u_{\tau,t})=\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that for any <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\left|m_{t}\right|\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\left|m_{t}\right|\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>, so
for <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}\leq 1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}\leq 1/T</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq t/T\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq t/T\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, since the set of meta-stepsizes includes <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}=1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}=1/T</annotation></semantics></math>,
the active set <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}=\left\{(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}_{{t-1}}:\eta_{j}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq 1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}=\left\{(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}_{{t-1}}:\eta_{j}(1+\left|m_{t}\right|)\leq 1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>
is never empty.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove that <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a valid probability
distribution, it suffices to show that <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and is supported
on <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, in this case we have that
<math id="A1.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}^{h}=\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}/\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}^{h}=\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}/\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}q_{t}^{h}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}q_{t}^{h}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, we will prove the following inductive hypotheses</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}F_{t}=0&amp;\text{if }S_{t}=0\\
F_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}\text{ with }\mathrm{supp}(F_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{{t-1}}&amp;S_{t}&gt;0\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}F_{t}=0&amp;\text{if }S_{t}=0\\
F_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{H}|}_{\geq 0}\text{ with }\mathrm{supp}(F_{t})=\mathcal{H}_{{t-1}}&amp;S_{t}&gt;0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
