<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each base algorithm <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(A,j)\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is specified by an algorithm
instance <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and a meta learning rate <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\ldots,J\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that by construction, we have that <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=(2J+3)(J+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=(2J+3)(J+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so for any <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}=\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl((2J+3)(J+1)\bigr)=O(\log\log(T))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}=\log\left|\mathcal{H}\right|=\log\bigl((2J+3)(J+1)\bigr)=O(\log\log(T)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for every <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{h}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{h}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
