<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General convex losses.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the Delayed OGD algorithm instance. Among the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J+1</annotation></semantics></math> base
algorithms associated with this instance, let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be the one
selected by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
By convexity of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
