<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">while <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> uses the elementary inequality
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sqrt{s}-\frac{\widehat{\lambda}}{2}s\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2\widehat{\lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sqrt{s}-\frac{\widehat{\lambda}}{2}s\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2\widehat{\lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=3G\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=3G\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}\geq\lambda/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}\geq\lambda/2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\leq 2G/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\leq 2G/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the base term, recall that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{SC}}(\widehat{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>SC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{SC}}(\widehat{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> is Delayed
FTRL run on the surrogate losses <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
These losses are <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex and satisfy
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}(x)=g_{t}+\widehat{\lambda}(x-x_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}(x)=g_{t}+\widehat{\lambda}(x-x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}\leq 2G/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}\leq 2G/D</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}(x)\|_{2}\leq G+\widehat{\lambda}D\leq 3G." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\lambda}}(x)\|_{2}\leq G+\widehat{\lambda}D\leq 3G.</annotation></semantics></math>
Therefore, applying the Delayed FTRL guarantee
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al., 2025</a>, Theorem 3.1]</cite> with gradient bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3G</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\widehat{\lambda}}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\widehat{\lambda}}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\lambda}\geq\lambda/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\lambda}\geq\lambda/2</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Combining this bound with <a href="#A2.E18" title="In Strongly convex losses. ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equations</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Strongly convex losses. ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}=\mathcal{O}(\log\log T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}=\mathcal{O}(\log\log T)</annotation></semantics></math>, the additive
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> term can be absorbed into the leading <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log T</annotation></semantics></math> term. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}\log\log T\right]\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{G^{2}}{\lambda}\left[\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}\log\log T\right]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">which proves <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Universal Regret Guarantee ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Exp-concave losses.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\coloneq\frac{1}{2}\min\{1/(4GD),\alpha\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\coloneq\frac{1}{2}\min\{1/(4GD),\alpha\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
First suppose
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&lt;(1/(8GD))2^{-J}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&lt;(1/(8GD))2^{-J}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\lceil\log_{2}T\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\lceil\log_{2}T\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{J}\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{J}\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\beta}&gt;8GD\,2^{J}\geq 8GDT." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\beta}&gt;8GD\,2^{J}\geq 8GDT.</annotation></semantics></math>
Moreover,
by <a href="#Thmlemma12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ Appendix D Supporting Lemmas ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> we have
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}\leq\frac{T(T-1)}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}\leq\frac{T(T-1)}{2},</annotation></semantics></math>
so the guarantee for the general convex case <a href="#S4.E3" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Universal Regret Guarantee ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)=\mathcal{O}\left(GD\,T\sqrt{H_{\rho}}+GD\,\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right)=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}{\beta}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)=\mathcal{O}\left(GD\,T\sqrt{H_{\rho}}+GD\,\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right)=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}{\beta}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the last relation uses <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and recalls <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\leq\frac{1}{8G\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\leq\frac{1}{8G\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the claimed exp-concave guarantee always holds in this case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to consider
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1/(8GD))2^{-J}\leq\beta\leq 1/(8GD)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1/(8GD))2^{-J}\leq\beta\leq 1/(8GD).</annotation></semantics></math>
By the construction of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\leq\beta&lt;2\widehat{\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\leq\beta&lt;2\widehat{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math>
For this <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the exp-concave surrogate
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\coloneq\left\langle g_{t},x\right\rangle+\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\coloneq\left\langle g_{t},x\right\rangle+\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Consider the base algorithm <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{EC}}(\widehat{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{EC}}(\widehat{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,
<a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> run on the surrogate sequence
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> with internal curvature parameter
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\beta}\coloneq\widehat{\beta}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\beta}\coloneq\widehat{\beta}/4</annotation></semantics></math>. Among the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J+1</annotation></semantics></math>
meta-experts associated with this base algorithm, let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be the
one selected by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Recall
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{h}\coloneq\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-x_{t}^{h}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{h}\coloneq\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-x_{t}^{h}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,
<a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 ( , , Lemma 3). ‣ Appendix D Supporting Lemmas ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> implies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(x_{t})-f_{t}(u)\leq\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(x_{t})-f_{t}(u)\leq\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle^{2}=z_{t}^{h}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}+f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x_{t}^{h})-f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}\left\langle g_{t},x_{t}-u\right\rangle^{2}=z_{t}^{h}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}+f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x_{t}^{h})-f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Summing over <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(z_{t}^{h}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}\right)}_{\eqcolon M_{T}^{h}}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x_{t}^{h})-f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(u)\right)}_{\eqcolon E_{T}^{h}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(z_{t}^{h}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}\right)}_{\eqcolon M_{T}^{h}}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x_{t}^{h})-f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(u)\right)}_{\eqcolon E_{T}^{h}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2. ‣ Algorithm design. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{T}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{T}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2GD\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2GD\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
