<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which
gives
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\sigma_{\max}^{+}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}(z_{t}^{h})^{2}\leq\sigma_{\max}^{+}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(z_{t}^{h})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math>
follows from the elementary inequality
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sqrt{s}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}s\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2\widehat{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sqrt{s}-\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{2}s\leq\frac{a^{2}}{2\widehat{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=3\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=3\sqrt{\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> uses
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\geq\beta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\geq\beta/2</annotation></semantics></math> and
recalls that
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="GD\leq 1/(8\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">GD\leq 1/(8\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> by definition of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the base term, recall that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\mathrm{EC}}(\widehat{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\mathrm{EC}}(\widehat{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> is
<a href="#algorithm2" title="In 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> run on the surrogate loss sequence
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)=\left(1+\widehat{\beta}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\right)g_{t},\qquad\nabla^{2}f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)=\widehat{\beta}g_{t}g_{t}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)=\left(1+\widehat{\beta}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\right)g_{t},\qquad\nabla^{2}f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)=\widehat{\beta}g_{t}g_{t}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\leq 1/(8GD)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\leq 1/(8GD)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\right|\leq GD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\right|\leq GD</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7/8\leq 1+\widehat{\beta}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\leq 9/8," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7/8\leq 1+\widehat{\beta}\left\langle g_{t},x-x_{t}\right\rangle\leq 9/8,</annotation></semantics></math>
and hence
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\|_{2}\leq(9/8)G." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\|_{2}\leq(9/8)G.</annotation></semantics></math>
Moreover,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla^{2}f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\succeq\frac{64}{81}\widehat{\beta}\,\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\succeq\frac{64}{81}\widehat{\beta}\,\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)\nabla f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}(x)^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}^{\widehat{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(64\widehat{\beta}/81)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>81</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(64\widehat{\beta}/81)</annotation></semantics></math>-exp-concave. Therefore, with gradient bound
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{EC}}\coloneq 9G/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{EC}}\coloneq 9G/8</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 ( , , Lemma 3). ‣ Appendix D Supporting Lemmas ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> guarantees the
quadratic curvature parameter</p>
<table id="A2.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\min\left\{\frac{1}{4G_{\mathrm{EC}}D},\frac{64}{81}\widehat{\beta}\right\}=\frac{32}{81}\widehat{\beta}&gt;\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{4}=\widetilde{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\min\left\{\frac{1}{4G_{\mathrm{EC}}D},\frac{64}{81}\widehat{\beta}\right\}=\frac{32}{81}\widehat{\beta}&gt;\frac{\widehat{\beta}}{4}=\widetilde{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">where we used <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\leq 1/(8GD)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\leq 1/(8GD)</annotation></semantics></math> in the equality.
Thus, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Improved Regret Bound for Exp-concave Losses ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> applies to the surrogate sequence
with curvature parameter <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\beta}=\widehat{\beta}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\beta}=\widehat{\beta}/4</annotation></semantics></math> and
gradient bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{EC}}=9G/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>EC</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{EC}}=9G/8</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</p>
<table id="A2.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\beta}}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\beta}}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\beta}=\widehat{\beta}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\beta}=\widehat{\beta}/4</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\beta}\geq\beta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\beta}\geq\beta/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{T}^{h}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Combining this bound with <a href="#A2.E21" title="In Exp-concave losses. ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equations</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Exp-concave losses. ‣ Appendix B Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}^{+}H_{\rho}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}=1+\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}=\mathcal{O}(\log\log T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}=\mathcal{O}(\log\log T)</annotation></semantics></math>,
the additive <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> term can be absorbed into the leading <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\log T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\log T</annotation></semantics></math> term.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}\log\log T\right]\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Reg}_{T}(u)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left[n\log T+\min\left\{\sigma_{\max}n\log T,\,\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}+\sigma_{\max}\log\log T\right]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">which proves <a href="#S4.E5" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Universal Regret Guarantee ‣ 4 Universal Regret with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
∎</p>
</div>
