<div id="A3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p19.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows that the cumulative comparator-gap change induced by delayed updates and time-varying regularization remains uniformly controlled. In particular, the total contribution is bounded by <math id="A3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{T}D^{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{T}D^{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, independently of the delay pattern.</p>
</div>
