<div id="A3.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now consider <math id="A3.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\tau&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\tau&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>; the case <math id="A3.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math> is immediate.
Consider the same process up to round <math id="A3.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, except that every
feedback from a round <math id="A3.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> that would arrive after round
<math id="A3.p43.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is instead revealed at the end of round <math id="A3.p43.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Since such
feedback is still unavailable when <math id="A3.p43.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen,
this modification leaves the algorithm unchanged up to the prediction
at round <math id="A3.p43.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="A3.p43.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p43.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p43.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{r,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{r,s}</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="A3.p43.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq s\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq s\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> are unchanged.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">To express the left-hand side of
<a href="#A3.E60" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a> for the modified process, partition
<math id="A3.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tau]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tau]</annotation></semantics></math> according to the sets <math id="A3.p44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{\tau+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{\tau+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p44.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\tau+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\tau+1}</annotation></semantics></math>
of the original process. If <math id="A3.p44.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in o_{\tau+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in o_{\tau+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="A3.p44.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+d_{r}\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+d_{r}\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, so the modification leaves its reveal time
unchanged; its contribution is therefore the same as in the original
process, with coefficient <math id="A3.p44.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{r,r+d_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{r,r+d_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> and Hessian
<math id="A3.p44.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\overline{H}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\overline{H}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.p44.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in m_{\tau+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in m_{\tau+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="A3.p44.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+d_{r}&gt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+d_{r}&gt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, so its feedback is instead revealed at the end of
round <math id="A3.p44.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in the modified process; its contribution therefore
uses coefficient <math id="A3.p44.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{r,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{r,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and Hessian
<math id="A3.p44.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}H_{r}+(\eta_{\tau}-\eta_{r-1})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}H_{r}+(\eta_{\tau}-\eta_{r-1})I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.p44.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{\tau+1}\cup m_{\tau+1}=[\tau]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{\tau+1}\cup m_{\tau+1}=[\tau]</annotation></semantics></math>, applying
<a href="#A3.E60" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Omitted Details from Section ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a> to the modified <math id="A3.p44.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-round process gives</span></p>
