<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Supporting Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show several auxiliary lemmas that are used throughout the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following standard lemma provides the quadratic bound of <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-exp-concave functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10</span></span><span id="Thmlemma10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hazan et al., 2007</a>, Lemma 3</cite>)<span id="Thmlemma10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Bounded domain and gradients). ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumptions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (𝛼-exp-concavity). ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> hold. Then, for any
<math id="Thmlemma10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}(x)\geq f_{t}(y)+\left\langle\nabla f_{t}(y),x-y\right\rangle+\frac{\beta}{2}\left\langle\nabla f_{t}(y),x-y\right\rangle^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}(x)\geq f_{t}(y)+\left\langle\nabla f_{t}(y),x-y\right\rangle+\frac{\beta}{2}\left\langle\nabla f_{t}(y),x-y\right\rangle^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{1}{2}\min\{1/(4GD),\alpha\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{1}{2}\min\{1/(4GD),\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemmas collect useful bounds on the delay quantities that will be used throughout the analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11</span></span><span id="Thmlemma11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every sequence of delays, the maximum number of missing observations satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\leq\min\left\{d_{\max},\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\leq\min\left\{d_{\max},\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma A.6 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al. [2025]</a></cite>,
<math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\leq\min_{S\subseteq[T]}\bigl(|S|+d_{\max}([T]\setminus S)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\leq\min_{S\subseteq[T]}\bigl(|S|+d_{\max}([T]\setminus S)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\leq d_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\leq d_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We next show <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\leq\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\leq\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following a counting argument similar to that used in the proof of Lemma A.7 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiu et al. [2025]</a></cite>, let <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}\in\argmax_{t\in[T]}|m_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}\in\argmax_{t\in[T]}|m_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m_{t^{\star}}|=\sigma_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m_{t^{\star}}|=\sigma_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in m_{t^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in m_{t^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the feedback from round <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> has not been observed by the beginning of round <math id="A4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+d_{t}\geq t^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+d_{t}\geq t^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{t}\geq t^{\star}-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{t}\geq t^{\star}-t</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}\geq\sum_{t\in m_{t^{\star}}}d_{t}\geq\sum_{t\in m_{t^{\star}}}(t^{\star}-t)\geq\sum_{i=1}^{|m_{t^{\star}}|}i=\frac{|m_{t^{\star}}|\bigl(|m_{t^{\star}}|+1\bigr)}{2}\geq\frac{\sigma_{\max}^{2}}{2}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}\geq\sum_{t\in m_{t^{\star}}}d_{t}\geq\sum_{t\in m_{t^{\star}}}(t^{\star}-t)\geq\sum_{i=1}^{|m_{t^{\star}}|}i=\frac{|m_{t^{\star}}|\bigl(|m_{t^{\star}}|+1\bigr)}{2}\geq\frac{\sigma_{\max}^{2}}{2}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the fourth inequality follows because the quantities <math id="A4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}-t</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in m_{t^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in m_{t^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, are distinct positive integers. Rearranging yields <math id="A4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\leq\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\leq\sqrt{2d_{\mathrm{tot}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows that the total delay is at most quadratic
in the horizon.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmlemma12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every sequence of delays such that <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+d_{t}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+d_{t}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that
<math id="Thmlemma12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}\leq\frac{T(T-1)}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}\leq\frac{T(T-1)}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}(T-t)=T^{2}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}t=T^{2}-\frac{T(T+1)}{2}=\frac{T(T-1)}{2}\;.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}(T-t)=T^{2}-\sum_{t=1}^{T}t=T^{2}-\frac{T(T+1)}{2}=\frac{T(T-1)}{2}\;.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows an important relation between the missing sets and
feedback sets, which we will use frequently throughout the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmlemma13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It holds that <math id="Thmlemma13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=m_{t+1}\cup\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=m_{t+1}\cup\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where both expressions are disjoint unions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the missing set at the beginning of round <math id="A4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{t}=\left\{s&lt;t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{t}=\left\{s&lt;t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}=\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}=t\right\}\cup\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}&gt;t\right\}=\mathcal{F}_{t}\cup m_{t+1}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{t}\cup\left\{t\right\}=\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}=\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}=t\right\}\cup\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}&gt;t\right\}=\mathcal{F}_{t}\cup m_{t+1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">The latter is a disjoint union because it simply partitions <math id="A4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{s\leq t:s+d_{s}\geq t\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> based on
whether the arrival time is exactly round <math id="A4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> or after <math id="A4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we define the delay interval for round t as <math id="A4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}=\left\{t,\ldots,t+d_{t}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}=\left\{t,\ldots,t+d_{t}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and we define <math id="A4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{t}=1+\max_{\tau\in I_{t}}\left|m_{\tau}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{t}=1+\max_{\tau\in I_{t}}\left|m_{\tau}\right|</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following lemma (<a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, restated here for clarity) provides two complementary controls on
<math id="A4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>-weighted quadratic terms, in terms of either the total delay
<math id="A4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math> or one plus the maximum number of missing observations <math id="A4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Desired guarantee. ‣ 3 Second-order Expert Aggregation with Delayed Feedback ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any round <math id="A4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="A4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, an observation that is missing
at round <math id="A4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> either was already missing at round <math id="A4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, or corresponds to
one of the rounds <math id="A4.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,t+1,\ldots,s-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,t+1,\ldots,s-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m_{s}|\leq|m_{t}|+(s-t)\leq|m_{t}|+d_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m_{s}|\leq|m_{t}|+(s-t)\leq|m_{t}|+d_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from <math id="A4.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the maximum over <math id="A4.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in I_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in I_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{t}=1+\max_{s\in I_{t}}|m_{s}|\leq 1+|m_{t}|+d_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{t}=1+\max_{s\in I_{t}}|m_{s}|\leq 1+|m_{t}|+d_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="A4.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}\leq T+\sum_{t=1}^{T}|m_{t}|+\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}=T+2d_{\mathrm{tot}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}\leq T+\sum_{t=1}^{T}|m_{t}|+\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}=T+2d_{\mathrm{tot}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the equality uses
<math id="A4.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}|m_{t}|=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}=d_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}|m_{t}|=\sum_{t=1}^{T}d_{t}=d_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, for any real sequence <math id="A4.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{t})_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{t})_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}z_{t}^{2}\leq\left(\max_{t\in[T]}z_{t}^{2}\right)\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}\leq(T+2d_{\mathrm{tot}})\max_{t\in[T]}z_{t}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}z_{t}^{2}\leq\left(\max_{t\in[T]}z_{t}^{2}\right)\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}\leq(T+2d_{\mathrm{tot}})\max_{t\in[T]}z_{t}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from <a href="#A4.E63" title="In Proof of . ‣ Appendix D Supporting Lemmas ‣ Universal Online Convex Optimization With Delayed Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>. Moreover,
<math id="A4.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{t}=\max_{s\in I_{t}}(|m_{s}|+1)\leq\max_{s\in[T]}(|m_{s}|+1)=\sigma_{\max}^{+}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{t}=\max_{s\in I_{t}}(|m_{s}|+1)\leq\max_{s\in[T]}(|m_{s}|+1)=\sigma_{\max}^{+},</annotation></semantics></math>
so we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}z_{t}^{2}\leq\sigma_{\max}^{+}\sum_{t=1}^{T}z_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\chi_{t}z_{t}^{2}\leq\sigma_{\max}^{+}\sum_{t=1}^{T}z_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p12.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p12.6.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the minimum of the previous two bounds concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>A Brief Review of ML-Prod</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard ML-Prod analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gaillard and Stoltz, 2014</a>]</cite> revolves around a certain log inequality—sometimes called the
Prod bound: <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)\geq x-x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that, starting from <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}=\mathrm{Uniform}(\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}=\mathrm{Uniform}(\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, ML-Prod
plays <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}\in\Delta(\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}\in\Delta(\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}^{h}\propto\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}^{h}\propto\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
and updates <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{h}=(\sum_{k}q_{t}^{k}\ell_{t}^{k})-\ell_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{h}=(\sum_{k}q_{t}^{k}\ell_{t}^{k})-\ell_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the excess loss of expert <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the loss <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{t}\in[0,1]^{|\mathcal{H}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{t}\in[0,1]^{|\mathcal{H}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, so long as <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}\geq-\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}\geq-\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> we have that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})=\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})=\log(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})\geq\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}-\eta_{h}^{2}(r_{t}^{h})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and thus, by re-arranging and summing over <math id="A5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="A5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}r_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex183.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h}/w_{t}^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\log(1/w_{1}^{h})-\log(1/w_{T+1}^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\log(1/w_{1}^{h})-\log(1/w_{T+1}^{h})}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\log(\left|\mathcal{H}\right|)}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\log(\left|\mathcal{H}\right|)}{\eta_{h}}+\eta_{h}\sum_{t=1}^{T}(r_{t}^{h})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the second line observes that
<math id="A5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl(\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h})-\log(w_{t}^{h})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl(\log(w_{{t+1}}^{h})-\log(w_{t}^{h})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">telescopes</em>
to <math id="A5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(w_{T+1}^{h})-\log(w_{1}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(w_{T+1}^{h})-\log(w_{1}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math> and the last line observes that <math id="A5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{T+1}^{h}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{T+1}^{h}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, since the
update <math id="A5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the total mass on each round:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex186.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\left(\sum_{k}\eta_{k}w_{t}^{k}\right)\sum_{h}q_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\left(\sum_{k}\eta_{k}w_{t}^{k}\right)\sum_{h}q_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The last step observes that <math id="A5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}q_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}q_{t}^{h}r_{t}^{h}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by definition of <math id="A5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, by induction we have that <math id="A5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{1}^{h}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{1}^{h}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and we also have that <math id="A5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>
on all rounds since <math id="A5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Together, these imply that <math id="A5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}^{h}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}^{h}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> on each round,
so in particular <math id="A5.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(w^{h}_{T+1})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(w^{h}_{T+1})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above argument also provides some insight into why this approach will pose difficulties
in the delayed feedback setting; we can no longer set <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}=w_{t}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}=w_{t}(1+\eta_{h}r_{t}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math> directly,
since <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is not necessarily observed at the end of round <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. If we instead observe
some previously delayed feedback <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> on round <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tau+d_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tau+d_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, we might hope to set
<math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}=w_{t}(1+\eta_{h}r_{\tau}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}=w_{t}(1+\eta_{h}r_{\tau}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, which would preserve the telescoping
property, but now the total mass is not preserved as above:
<math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{t}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
and we do not necessarily have
<math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{t}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=0</annotation></semantics></math>
whenever <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\tau}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\tau}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, if we instead update <math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{\tau}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{\tau}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{{t+1}}^{h}=w_{\tau}^{h}(1+\eta_{h}r_{\tau}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}w_{{t+1}}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}+\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=\sum_{h}w_{\tau}^{h},</annotation></semantics></math>
since <math id="A5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>τ</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}\eta_{h}w_{\tau}^{h}r_{\tau}^{h}=0</annotation></semantics></math> but now the
log-ratio sum <math id="A5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\log(w_{{t+1}}/w_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\log(w_{{t+1}}/w_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> no longer telescopes.
In addition, observe that both of these tentative arguments would completely ignore the further issue of handling the simultaneous arrival of feedback from <em id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multiple</em> past rounds.</p>
